  "title": "BCIT Baseline Driving",
  "description": "This dataset contains EEG and driving performance data from the Baseline Driving study, part of the BCIT program investigating fatigue-related biomarkers during simulated driving tasks. Subjects performed a 60-minute driving task with EEG recorded at three different sites using varying channel configurations (64 or 256-channel Biosemi systems). The dataset supports research into predictive algorithms for detecting driver fatigue through EEG analysis and objective performance measures.",
  "methods_description": "Subjects performed a driving task using a simulator with steering wheel and pedal controls, and EEG data was recorded using BioSemi systems with up to 256 channels at a sampling rate of 1024 Hz. Eye tracking data were collected but not included in the dataset. The Baseline Driving task consisted of 60 minutes of driving in 6 blocks, during which subjects controlled speed and steering while responding to lateral perturbations.",
